Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:12:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] perf(blocks): cache wood wall and pipe shapes per block
 state

WoodWall rebuilt its outline and collision shapes on every query (four
BlockState.toString() calls plus up to four unions), and APipe did up to
twelve unions per outline query. Both results depend only on the block
state, so add a small ShapeCache that runs the unchanged computation once
per state and returns that result afterwards. The cache is a
ConcurrentHashMap because shapes are also queried from chunk builder
threads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TD7PJ5R7t7hM3ymeeqXP4H
